// Spec 2d (m-sources-sub.png): a "Tracks" row first inside a rekordbox drive,
// listing every track in the drive's export. The actual import (parseDeviceDB
// with Kaitai and SQLite) reads a fake export.pdb: seven tracks, tracks 1-4
// in the playlists Warm-up and Sets › Peak time, tracks 5-7 in none. The
// actual RekordboxFeature methods run on stand-ins: the sidebar model (a
// QAbstractItemModel over the real TreeItems), the table model (the list it
// shows, read with the join BaseExternalPlaylistModel reads) and the track
// collection (a SQLite file). The stand-in feature wires its signals as the
// RekordboxFeature constructor does. tests/native/drive_tracks_row_runner.py
// builds this; BASELINE is the source without mixxx-drive-tracks-row.patch.
